From 87056ab17f667853184672c4aa9220391c4d7cf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 08:08:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: Dolby Vision page and player rows that fit and read
 correctly

Measured with Estuary's font (Noto Sans at 33 px for font14) against the
885-pixel labels, several rows were cut with an ellipsis:
- The output row put the reason why native output is not used after
  "Ordinary Kodi output, without Dolby Vision:", 1200 to 1690 pixels in
  every language: the reason was never visible. The reason now has its
  own row ("Reason"/"Motivo"), shown only without native output, with
  shorter texts; the mode reason names the 24-60 Hz range.
- The layers row with the FEL counter, and the Spanish "Last 10 s" row
  even with ordinary values. The FEL counter has its own row, and the
  longest gap and L1 changes share a row apart from L5.
- The Spanish cache and queue row of the Player tab (about 1090
  pixels). The cache row is Estuary's own again; the video and audio
  buffers have their own row.

The FEL counter also came out garbled ("FEL residual240 / 240 last 10
s:"): $LOCALIZE is expanded before $INFO is split at commas, and its
label contained one. No label used inside $INFO contains a comma now.

The OSD button that opens the player information gets its help text,
and the Spanish row labels start with a capital letter like the others.
The widest row is now 852 pixels (en_gb, es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
